 n\nDoors at 6pm. Performances start at 6:30pm.\n\nCantor Arts Center prese
 nts Forms & Frequencies\, a Thursday night music series featuring musician
 s and sound artists from the Bay Area and beyond.\n\nJoin us on Thursday\,
  December 3 for a night of pounding electronics and unruly physicality wit
 h Xina Xurner and Tzotzona\, with visuals by artist Christopher Richmond.\
 n\nXina Xurner is a Los Angeles-based sadical and sexperimental music and 
 performance duo with vocalist\, sculptor\, and performance artist Young Jo
 on Kwak and musician and producer Marvin Astorga. Fusing industrial noise\
 , power electronics\, dark club-wrecking beats\, electric guitar\, and ext
 reme vocal distortion\, their body-shaking live shows unleash queer trans-
 femme rage\, refusal\, and joy.\n\nCreating an atmosphere that feels part 
 club\, part collective exorcism\, Xina Xurner’s performance will be pair
 ed with visuals by artist Christopher Richmond\, whose alien and terrestri
 al landscapes juxtapose reality and illusion\, using handmade props\, spec
 ial photography\, and varied drawing styles to present multiple pictorial 
 universes in constant kinetic interaction.\n\nTzotzona\, Astorga’s solo 
 project\, will open the evening with brown-futurist electronic music that 
 synthesizes elements of Cumbia\, Technobanda\, house\, techno\, acid\, Que
 bradita\, and 3bal. Taking inspiration and samples from Astorga’s upbrin
 ging in the El Paso-Ciudad Juárez Borderplex\, a pre-Columbian imaginary\
